\title{DynCount: Bayesian Dynamic Models for Count Time Series}
\description{
The \pkg{DynCount} package fits state-space models for non-Gaussian
time series. A latent trajectory \eqn{z_t} follows flexible dynamics --
a first-order random walk or a stationary AR(1) process -- and the
observations are linked to it through a Poisson (log link), a binomial
(logit link) or a multinomial (additive-log-ratio link) observation
model. An optional known \code{offset} may be added to the observation model's
linear predictor (a log-exposure for the Poisson mean, a logit shift for
the binomial probability, per-category ALR shifts for the multinomial
shares). This is a fixed, user-supplied input and is not part of the latent
process \eqn{z_t}.
}
\details{
The package implements and extends the methodology of Zens and Bijak
(2026, \doi{10.1214/26-AOAS2171}). It supports several innovation
structures (Gaussian, Student-t, finite scale mixture, stochastic
volatility) and, for the Poisson and binomial families, zero inflation with
a time-constant gate-open probability.
}
